  "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(n):\\frac{n}{10}\\in N,\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\u2203n\\in N,\\,P(n).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u2203n\\in N,\\,P(n))\u2261\u2200n\\in N,\\,\u00acP(n).\n$$\n\nFinally, $\u2200n\\in N,\\,\u00acP(n)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $n\\in N,$ $\\frac{n}{10}\\text{\\boldsymbol}\\notin N.$",
